Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:12.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Support us and become VIP member \Nto remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.57,0:03:41.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Look out, Mr. Potato Head!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.03,0:03:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Speck!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.10,0:04:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Me, too. Come on.\NLet's get some breakfast.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.46,0:05:10.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Mad dog!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.43,0:06:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Pee-wee.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.27,0:06:53.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Mr. Breakfast.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.44,0:06:56.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Can I have my "Mr. T" cereal?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.64,0:07:03.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I pity the poor fool\Nwho don't eat my cereal!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.01,0:07:34.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, Speck.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.91,0:07:38.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Welp, I'm off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.18,0:07:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You be good.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.13,0:08:00.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Mr. Crabtree.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.17,0:08:02.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Pee-wee.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.67,0:08:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to water my lawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.07,0:09:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning. I'm here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.36,0:09:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the best bike in the whole world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.98,0:09:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Brush-brush-brush.\NBrush-brush-brush.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.04,0:11:30.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I meant to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.36,0:12:55.72,Default,,0,0,0,,My good friend, Pee-wee!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.02,0:12:57.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, Mario.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.83,0:12:59.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you just browsing today?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.36,0:13:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Sort of. I wanted to stock up\Non some supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.66,0:13:04.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Help yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.44,0:13:11.74,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you like school?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.24,0:13:13.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.28,0:13:24.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.87,0:13:41.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I got some new items\Nyou might be interested in.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.91,0:13:55.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Box for Pee-wee.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.65,0:13:59.09,Default,,0,0,0,,New, improved, squirting flower.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.82,0:14:03.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Fake blood, or is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.26,0:14:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Super stink-bomb?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.99,0:14:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Have some.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.30,0:14:09.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Shrunken head?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.17,0:14:13.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Regular size?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.24,0:14:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Trick gum?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.01,0:14:26.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Headlight glasses?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.95,0:14:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And direct from Australia,\NThe Boomerang Bow-Tie!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.99,0:14:34.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Come in red?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.70,0:14:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be right back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.32,0:15:08.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-What's up, man?\N-How's it going?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.42,0:15:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Is Dottie still working on your bike?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.66,0:15:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I've got it back already.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.36,0:15:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,What's she doing to it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.83,0:15:18.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't talk about it.\NJames Bond kind of stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.97,0:15:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Dottie's radical with bikes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.44,0:15:24.100,Default,,0,0,0,,I say we cruise, dudes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.91,0:15:26.100,Default,,0,0,0,,It's getting hot in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.61,0:15:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It's steamy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.31,0:15:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sweating.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.68,0:15:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Is my horn ready yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.62,0:15:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,It's ready. It should be\Nloud enough for you now.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.95,0:15:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is it? Let's hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.69,0:15:47.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait. I want to talk to you first.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.56,0:15:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You are talking to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.56,0:15:51.55,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I want your undivided attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.07,0:15:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,This is important.\NI want to ask you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.08,0:16:03.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to know,\Nif you will do something?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.08,0:16:05.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.21,0:16:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to know if you'll\Ngo someplace with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.88,0:16:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Like where?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.59,0:16:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The drive-in.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.09,0:16:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, Dottie, I like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.63,0:16:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Like! I like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.16,0:16:22.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I like you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.57,0:16:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,There are a lot of things about me\Nyou don't know anything about.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.60,0:16:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Things you wouldn't understand,\Nyou couldn't understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.91,0:16:34.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Things you shouldn't understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.61,0:16:37.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.85,0:16:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't want to get mixed up with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.12,0:16:43.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a Ioner, Dottie. A rebel.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.62,0:16:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,So long, Dot.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.48,0:17:48.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you the owner?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.82,0:17:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. That's me. They call me Chuck.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.92,0:17:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Can I do anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.59,0:17:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,We're losing time!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.59,0:17:59.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Set up a dragnet!\NComb the whole area! Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.86,0:18:04.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid we can't consider your bike\Nbeing stolen a police emergency.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.33,0:18:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,If it doesn't turn up, come to\Nthe station and fill out a report.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.00,0:18:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the best we can do.\NCome on, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.21,0:18:15.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.84,0:18:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,To find my bike!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.19,0:19:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Why exactly do you believe\Nthe Soviets were involved?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.37,0:19:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me be honest. Hundreds of bikes\Nare stolen every month.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.37,0:19:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Very few of them are recovered.\NWe don't have the resources.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.21,0:19:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You're saying you can't do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.98,0:19:58.04,Default,,0,0,0,,My bike means everything to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.81,0:20:00.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew the police wouldn't help.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.05,0:20:03.04,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what I'd do?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.55,0:20:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Retrace my steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.82,0:20:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I parked my bike and\Nwhen I came back it was gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.22,0:20:13.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you think of anyone\Nwho'd want to take it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.39,0:20:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone wanted my bike.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.56,0:20:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Cash only.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.76,0:20:18.25,Default,,0,0,0,,No cards, no checks.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.59,0:20:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You got cash?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.80,0:20:25.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me take your jacket.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.53,0:20:30.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You want to wear a wet jacket,\Nit's all right with Madam Ruby.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.44,0:20:38.10,Default,,0,0,0,,For $20 I can tell you a lot of things.\NFor $30 I can tell you more.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.44,0:20:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,And for $50 I can tell you everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.78,0:20:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me why I'm here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.45,0:20:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,You're here because you...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.62,0:20:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,...want something.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.30,0:20:59.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.53,0:21:02.80,Default,,0,0,0,,...what Madam Ruby sees.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.38,0:21:10.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.48,0:21:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,...a bicycle.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.91,0:21:14.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes! Is it okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.65,0:21:15.94,Default,,0,0,0,,It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.98,0:21:19.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is it?! Can you see it?\NWhere is it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.32,0:21:22.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.09,0:21:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It's somewhere else.\NSomewhere far away.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.33,0:21:28.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Where?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.17,0:21:39.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The Alamo.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.68,0:21:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,The Alamo.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.95,0:21:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,In the basement.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.05,0:21:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll never forget you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.45,0:22:59.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks a million.\NI've been trying all day.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.36,0:23:09.59,Default,,0,0,0,,-The name's Mickey.\N-I'm Pee-wee.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.40,0:23:18.27,Default,,0,0,0,,How about some music?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.94,0:23:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Morelli is armed and dangerous...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.74,0:23:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Forget the music.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.64,0:23:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's enjoy the scenery.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.12,0:23:33.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What did you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.03,0:23:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I lost my temper, took a knife\Nand I...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.10,0:23:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You know those "Do not remove under\Npenalty of law" labels on mattresses?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.64,0:23:51.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I cut one off.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.64,0:23:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I got a real bad temper.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.44,0:23:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I always thought that was a dumb law.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.08,0:24:01.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You said a mouthful.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.72,0:24:04.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Life can be so unfair.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.62,0:24:06.52,Default,,0,0,0,,You're telling me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.70,0:25:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I tried to go through legal channels.\NBut the cops, hah!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.01,0:25:05.04,Default,,0,0,0,,They were no help.\NThey gave me the runaround.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.25,0:25:09.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That's when I decided to take\Nthe law into my own hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.85,0:25:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The law...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:11.72,0:25:13.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The law.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.39,0:25:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The law.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.86,0:25:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,The law!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.83,0:25:19.69,Default,,0,0,0,,This is it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.66,0:25:23.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I got an idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.24,0:25:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.74,0:25:36.90,Default,,0,0,0,,We're looking for an escaped convict.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.24,0:25:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,We heard about it on the radio.\NRight, honey?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.98,0:25:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you seen this man?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.75,0:25:48.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I've seen better heads on boils!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.29,0:25:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I'm sure I'd remember this face.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.36,0:25:59.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-Would you mind stepping out of the car.\N-No, not at all, officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.60,0:26:02.97,Default,,0,0,0,,-Some sort of problem?\N-Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.10,0:26:05.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted to look at\Nthat cute outfit you have on.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.51,0:26:13.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you take a picture?\NIt'll last longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.79,0:26:25.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You have a nice day.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.03,0:27:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,What's it like in the big house, Mickey?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.90,0:27:11.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not so bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.44,0:27:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You get to lift weights,\Nwatch TV, write up appeals...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.18,0:27:18.84,Default,,0,0,0,,...take long showers, lift weights.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.65,0:27:22.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You get used to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.85,0:28:31.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Out!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:32.15,0:28:33.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Out!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:34.89,0:28:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It wasn't my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.42,0:28:39.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Look kid, I like you. I like you a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.93,0:28:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I can't drag you into this.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.26,0:28:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm bad. You don't get mixed up\Nwith a guy like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.93,0:28:47.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a Ioner. A rebel!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.50,0:28:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,D�j� vu.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.00,0:28:52.97,Default,,0,0,0,,See you in the Promised Land.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.21,0:28:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Arrivederci, baby!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:00.35,0:29:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.28,0:29:06.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm in the middle of nowhere!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.96,0:29:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure is spooky out here.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:28.97,0:29:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably just a dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.22,0:29:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Kitty.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:50.30,0:29:52.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's those headlight glasses?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.34,0:30:31.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the San Antonio Department\Nof Parks and Recreation Alamo tour.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.34,0:30:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,My name is Tina.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.31,0:30:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me Tina,\Nbut could we go straight...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:36.84,0:30:40.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's hold all questions\Nuntil the end of the tour.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.25,0:30:42.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.42,0:30:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,This Mission, the Alamo, named from\Nthe Spanish word for cottonwood tree...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.32,0:30:50.26,Default,,0,0,0,,...was established in the year 1718.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.66,0:30:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The same year that our city was founded\Nby the Spanish expeditionary force...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.50,0:30:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,...on the site of\Nan Indian burial mound.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.73,0:31:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,This is one of my favorite parts\Nof the tour.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.87,0:31:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Please say hello to our residents,\NPedro and his wife, Inez.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.41,0:31:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Inez is holding a clay pot\Nthat she seems very proud of.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.01,0:31:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,She carefully detailed it\Nwith paint and glaze.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.58,0:31:16.95,Default,,0,0,0,,And Pedro is working on an "adobe."
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.18,0:31:20.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you say that with me? Adobe.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.69,0:31:26.45,Default,,0,0,0,,We are now in the kitchen\Nof the Alamo women.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.86,0:31:30.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Here they are preparing\Nculinary delights of the Southwest.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.70,0:31:32.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Do I hear someone's stomach growling?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.04,0:31:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The mainstay of the Alamo diet is corn.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.04,0:31:40.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Corn can be prepared many ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:40.37,0:31:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It can be boiled, shucked,\Ncreamed...
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.81,0:31:45.64,Default,,0,0,0,,...or in this case dried.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.28,0:31:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Corn can also be used to make...
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.95,0:31:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,...tortillas.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:50.48,0:31:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Do we have any Mexican-Americans\Nwith us today?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.13,0:32:01.39,Default,,0,0,0,,There are thousands and thousands\Nof uses for corn...
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.73,0:32:04.39,Default,,0,0,0,,...all of which I will\Ntell you about right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.90,0:32:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Upon this battlement, in 1836...
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.73,0:32:09.40,Default,,0,0,0,,...two hundred Texas volunteers...
Dialogue: 0,0:32:09.74,0:32:13.90,Default,,0,0,0,,...including such heroes as\NDavy Crockett, Bill Travis, Jim Bowie...
Dialogue: 0,0:32:14.24,0:32:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,...fought off an onslaught\Nof 4,000 Mexicans...
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.58,0:32:21.41,Default,,0,0,0,,...under the command of\NGeneral Antonio Lopez de Santa Ana.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.55,0:32:25.78,Default,,0,0,0,,At this time, I'd like\Nto conclude our tour.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:25.92,0:32:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You all have been one of the greatest\Ngroups I have ever worked with.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.76,0:32:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Are there any questions?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.19,0:32:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the basement?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.76,0:32:38.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Aren't we going to see the basement?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:39.77,0:32:42.10,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no basement at the Alamo.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.48,0:33:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Pee-wee, I'm on my way to Paris.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.82,0:33:36.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Andy and I had a fight after you left.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:36.66,0:33:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You were right, Pee-wee.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.29,0:33:40.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm making my wish come true.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:40.99,0:33:43.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm off to Paris!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.27,0:33:47.100,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.24,0:33:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Bus 91, leaving for New York City,\Nnow departing.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:51.34,0:33:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,That's my bus.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.71,0:33:55.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.38,0:34:00.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess what. The Alamo was built\Nwithout a basement.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.35,0:34:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.82,0:34:05.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither did I. They don't tell you\Nthat stuff in school.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.69,0:34:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It's something you\Njust have to experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.36,0:34:14.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry, Pee-wee.\NI know you'll find your bike.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.04,0:34:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck. I just know\Nyou're going to find your bike.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.24,0:34:58.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello, Dottie? It's me, Pee-wee.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.24,0:35:00.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you calling from?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.91,0:35:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Texas.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.14,0:35:05.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Honest. Listen, I'll prove it.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:05.88,0:35:09.41,Default,,0,0,0,,"The stars at night\NAre big and bright...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.92,0:35:12.91,Default,,0,0,0,,"Deep in the heart of Texas."
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.59,0:35:16.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait. Don't hang up.\NThere's something...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.22,0:35:18.42,Default,,0,0,0,,...I have to talk to you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.49,0:35:21.26,Default,,0,0,0,,It's about the other night.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:22.53,0:35:26.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I owe everybody a big apology.\NEspecially you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.77,0:35:30.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't mean what I said, Dottie.\NHonest.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.27,0:35:32.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.07,0:35:35.54,Default,,0,0,0,,There's somebody else\Nwho's been worried about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:42.12,0:35:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.92,0:35:46.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I forgot.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.62,0:35:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Speck!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.63,0:35:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Speck! Put Dottie back on.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:00.47,0:36:02.63,Default,,0,0,0,,There's something I want to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.37,0:36:07.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I've learned something\Nout here on the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:08.18,0:36:08.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Humility.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.15,0:36:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Dottie, when I get back,\Nwill you...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.88,0:36:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,What, Pee-wee?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.69,0:36:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you still help me find my bike?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.59,0:36:25.65,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.39,0:36:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,There's something else\NI wanted to ask you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.40,0:36:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.70,0:36:34.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Could you wire me a bus ticket?\NI'll pay you back. Honest.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.34,0:36:37.20,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Pee-wee.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:37.27,0:36:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,When you get back,\Nwe can settle up at the drive-in.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.41,0:36:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.41,0:36:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn't hear that last part.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.51,0:36:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,The connection just got really bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.42,0:36:50.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.43,0:37:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:01.26,0:37:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.70,0:37:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Where you from?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:05.70,0:37:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.67,0:37:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't you remember anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.50,0:37:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember the Alamo.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.04,0:37:47.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, operator. I can't hear you.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.05,0:37:54.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm trying to use the phone!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.33,0:38:04.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:03.72,0:39:05.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Break dance!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.13,0:39:44.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Tequila!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:58.45,0:40:00.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks a lot, dudes.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.42,0:40:04.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope you find your bike.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:33.100,0:40:37.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The customized bicycle was presented\Nto child star, Kevin Morton...
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.33,0:40:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,...at Warner Brothers Studios\Nin Hollywood, California.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:43.04,0:40:44.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations, Kevin.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:44.84,0:40:46.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Mr. Hawthorne.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:46.47,0:40:48.74,Default,,0,0,0,,A bike like this is every boy's dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.63,0:41:15.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, sir.\NDo you have a pass?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.54,0:41:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no, I' sorry you can't\Nenter without a pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.47,0:41:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,So the fellow said, "What do you think\NI have down here, a duck?"
Dialogue: 0,0:41:30.02,0:41:31.38,Default,,0,0,0,,A duck!
Dialogue: 0,0:41:52.27,0:41:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Where can I find Kevin Morton?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.98,0:41:58.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:58.88,0:42:01.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know what stage\NKevin Morton is on?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.88,0:42:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It's stage six.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.42,0:42:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. I want to go once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.91,0:42:28.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hair standing by.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.95,0:42:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What I want to do now,\Nis I want to do one more, faster paced.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:36.58,0:42:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Kevin?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:37.52,0:42:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, I would love to...
Dialogue: 0,0:42:39.12,0:42:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,...except how can I\Nwhen she's so late on her cues?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:42.96,0:42:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:47.99,0:42:48.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Marion.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.03,0:42:53.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't have to take that\Nfrom that little...
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.14,0:42:56.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Kid! He's just a kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.27,0:42:59.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Even a kid can be courteous.\NI'm going to quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:59.81,0:43:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear it, I am going to quit!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:03.68,0:43:06.20,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Jerry. But I have had it!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.32,0:43:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, is everything straightened out?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:11.49,0:43:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,We're ready when you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.05,0:43:15.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Doesn't it look like I'm ready?!\NI am always ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:16.16,0:43:20.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I have been ready since first call!\NI am ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.69,0:43:21.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:22.50,0:43:24.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Quiet, please! This is a take!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.57,0:43:28.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Action!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.30,0:43:31.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Good-bye, Mother Superior.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:32.27,0:43:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Good-bye, Rusty. And God bless you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.91,0:43:41.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you Mother Superior,\NI want the orphanage to have my bike.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.35,0:43:42.58,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Rusty.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:42.85,0:43:46.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You sold a lot of magazine subscriptions\Nto earn that bike.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:46.85,0:43:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,But I want to give.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:49.79,0:43:54.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I've just received the two best parents\Na boy could ever hope for.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:54.89,0:43:59.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Rusty, you are an inspiration to us all.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.57,0:44:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll say.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:01.40,0:44:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to start\Na paper route right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:08.54,0:44:10.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop that nun!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:17.89,0:44:20.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember me? Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.27,0:46:49.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Merry Christmas!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:58.88,0:49:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Geronimo!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:10.02,0:49:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Radical!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:42.72,0:49:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You can help me. Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:44.79,0:49:46.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't panic!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:46.36,0:49:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,No pushing, no shoving.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:49.56,0:49:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Move in an orderly fashion\Nto the front exit.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:03.24,0:50:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Stay!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:04.74,0:50:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen up, everybody! Sit!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:24.76,0:50:25.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.11,0:50:38.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on! Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:45.62,0:50:48.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Fast! Come on! Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:38.37,0:51:41.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Son, are you all right?\NCan you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:41.44,0:51:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,There's still a few more fish inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:44.64,0:51:45.94,Default,,0,0,0,,This boy is a hero.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:46.18,0:51:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,This boy is under arrest.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:05.33,0:52:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I can explain, Mr. Hawthorne.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:07.97,0:52:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Call me "Terry."
Dialogue: 0,0:52:12.50,0:52:15.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Warner Brothers thinks your story\Nwould make a fantastic movie.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:16.07,0:52:18.41,Default,,0,0,0,,My story. A movie?!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:25.32,0:52:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,My bike!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:34.39,0:52:35.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Do we have a deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:09.13,0:53:11.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Pee-wee, can I have your autograph?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.37,0:53:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's your chili dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:27.21,0:53:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Pee-wee! Over here. Look! Box seats!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.75,0:53:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Bob, Luke, Skinny and Milton.\NBoys, this is Pee-wee!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:38.05,0:53:39.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Sno-cones.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:40.06,0:53:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I never met a movie star.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:43.89,0:53:45.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What did they pay you?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:47.80,0:53:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:08.28,0:54:10.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's take a breather, Dottie.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:10.55,0:54:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The X-1 needs to cool down.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:14.42,0:54:16.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a little overheated myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.53,0:54:20.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Come over here, P.W.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:01.64,0:55:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I must get to a phone.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:13.15,0:55:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Great so far, Pee-wee.\NAction packed.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:16.65,0:55:18.05,Default,,0,0,0,,One soda.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:18.99,0:55:21.65,Default,,0,0,0,,One foot-Iong!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:29.07,0:55:30.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Good try, Pee-wee.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:41.55,0:55:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you got any message for Room 104?\NThe name is Herman.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:46.42,0:55:47.91,Default,,0,0,0,,P.W. Herman.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:53.86,0:55:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,No, nothing right now, Mr. Herman.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:59.53,0:56:01.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be in the bar.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:07.20,0:56:09.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That's fantastic!
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.88,0:56:22.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Ditto.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:22.39,0:56:24.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I brought you guys French fries!
Dialogue: 0,0:56:35.23,0:56:37.56,Default,,0,0,0,,The big scene's coming up, guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:56:47.24,0:56:49.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Paging Mr. Herman.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:49.58,0:56:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Herman, you have a telephone call\Nat the front desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:08.83,0:57:10.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:13.34,0:57:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That was the president.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:15.01,0:57:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I must steal back the X-1...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:16.77,0:57:20.11,Default,,0,0,0,,...before the Soviets find\Nthe hidden microfilm inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:20.84,0:57:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The future of the free world\Nis riding on this.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:23.78,0:57:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,-I'll go with you.\N-No, it's too dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:28.42,0:57:31.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I invented the X-1.\NI'm going with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.76,0:57:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.96,0:57:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You are such a pushover.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.76,0:57:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you are...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:40.93,0:57:42.36,Default,,0,0,0,,...but what am I?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:52.04,0:57:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations, Pee-wee!
Dialogue: 0,0:57:55.01,0:57:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, P.W.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:57.65,0:57:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,How's the X-1?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:59.32,0:58:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's cooled down. But I'm heated up.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:02.99,0:58:05.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's my candy?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:05.82,0:58:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I forgot.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:11.89,0:58:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Pee-wee and I go way back.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.83,0:58:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,When did you become blood brothers?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:16.67,0:58:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't remember the exact year.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:18.67,0:58:21.16,Default,,0,0,0,,And you say you taught Pee-wee\Nto ride his bike?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:21.87,0:58:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember the day I took off\Nhis training wheels.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.61,0:58:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the bike.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:29.01,0:58:30.84,Default,,0,0,0,,How about a picture of me on it?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:31.08,0:58:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think that's a good idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:32.75,0:58:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not your decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:35.35,0:58:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,If it wasn't for me, none of this\Nwould have happened to you, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:40.36,0:58:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, sort of.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:42.36,0:58:45.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Then it's okay if I sit on it.\NRight, Pee-wee?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:47.86,0:58:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Pee-wee, everybody's waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:57.04,0:58:58.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone, gather around.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:58.51,0:59:01.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me show you some of\Nthe more high-tech features.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:18.49,0:59:20.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't want to get mixed up with me.
